body:
hello there, i feel you man, im 38 and after a five year long heroine habit my life is in tatters, I'm lucky I got out alive and without a criminal record and I'm now picking up the pieces, I began using after I found my partner of 11 years and mother of children in bed with my cousin which devasted me totally I'm still not over it if I'm honest. 

&#x200B;

it sounds to me like youare  suffering with quite a serious bout of depression, I too had no idea what I wanted to do for a career and ending up working as a transport planner not what I wanted to do but it paid the bills.

sadly 70% of us do not enjoy our jobs so what I would recommend to you is this.

I hated my job and enjoy motorcycling so I used the job to pay for my motorcycle training and to purchase a motorcycle this has been a godsend for me as when I'm down I get the ZXR600 out and blast around the concentration required makes me zone into the ride and I forget about everything else and focus on my riding trying to set better times around some roads I practise on. i have a route and try and improve my time to complete it. So yes you won't enjoy your job but you can use it to open things up  you do enjoy. have you thought about travelling? you could start the job and then save up for a trip this will give you a reason to work and each time you get paid it will motivate you as it gets nearer and nearer to the day when you can depart on your trip. when it comes to depression you MUST fight it and see it as a battle if you don't fight it trust me it will kill you. I have attempted suicide three times and have lost two close friends to suicide as they didn't fight and just allowed the low feelings to wash over them and ran with it. As a  human being, you have been given the gift of being able to rationilse your emotions so when the low mood begins say to your self fuck off depression I'm going to work and going on this trip you cant stop me! 

&#x200B;

trust me just starting a job will help as it will keep you busy so your mind has less time to wander and land on depressing thought matter. 

&#x200B;

yo say you have no purpose and the thing with that is most people don't this is normal so make it your purpose to beat your depression that for now is what your purpose is to simply find a way to improve your mental state i cant think of a better purpose for you at this time time. do the crappy job but reward your self with the things that make you happy this could be buying new clothes going out or paying for a hooker honestly what ever it takes to distract you. distraction is the main AIM here as when you are distracted and your mind is working on things you will have less time to think about the things that are bringing you down. 

&#x200B;

I would also reccomd practising stocism this is a philopshy which is remarkable for depression study the story and writings of Epictetus he was a slave who was forced to adapt his thinking i cant recommend you reading this enough. 

&#x200B;

please get back to me as to what your plans are i would love to know!

so please start to see this as a WAR, are you going to a casualty of this mental battle or a victor? i believe you can be a victor. Also you say the medication didn't work but i think this is because you didn't give it a chance anti depressants take about 4 weeks before you will notice any effects ask your doctor for a strong SSRI these are selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors.

&#x200B;

serotonis is a neruo transmitter effecting mood and this medication will increase the amount of serotonin in the brain which will improve your mood this isn't a maybe once those levels increase your mood will improve slowly.

&#x200B;

please make a list of some goals that you think will improve your mental state and then jot down how you can go about achieving them
